.TH EB\-STAGED\-REBUILD "1" "2026\-11\-26" "eb\-staged\-rebuild" "eb\-staged\-rebuild Manual"
.SH NAME
eb\-staged\-rebuild
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B eb\-staged\-rebuild
[-h] [--version] {probe,run,resume,verify,rollback,gc,retire,status,list,resolve} ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Build EasyBuild software in a staged tree, then exchange the complete tree with the stable live directory.

.SH
POSITIONAL ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fBeb\-staged\-rebuild\fR \fI\,probe\/\fR
report bwrap, user namespaces, RENAME_EXCHANGE, and EasyBuild
.TP
\fBeb\-staged\-rebuild\fR \fI\,run\/\fR
build and atomically swap a staged tree
.TP
\fBeb\-staged\-rebuild\fR \fI\,resume\/\fR
continue a run after a crash
.TP
\fBeb\-staged\-rebuild\fR \fI\,verify\/\fR
check a built run's stage before it is published
.TP
\fBeb\-staged\-rebuild\fR \fI\,rollback\/\fR
switch back to the previous generation or a named one, or put a retired module file back
.TP
\fBeb\-staged\-rebuild\fR \fI\,gc\/\fR
remove hidden retired siblings after the grace period
.TP
\fBeb\-staged\-rebuild\fR \fI\,retire\/\fR
move a module file out of the module tree after its package is published elsewhere
.TP
\fBeb\-staged\-rebuild\fR \fI\,status\/\fR
show run journals
.TP
\fBeb\-staged\-rebuild\fR \fI\,list\/\fR
show each install path's live tree and the generations kept beside it
.TP
\fBeb\-staged\-rebuild\fR \fI\,resolve\/\fR
print the install path a module file names

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'eb\-staged\-rebuild probe'\/\fR
usage: eb\-staged\-rebuild probe [\-h] [\-\-path PATH] [\-\-no\-create] [\-\-eb EB]
                               [\-\-require\-eb] [\-\-json]

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'eb\-staged\-rebuild probe'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-path\fR \fI\,PATH\/\fR
directory on the filesystem to probe (default: .)

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-create\fR
refuse when \-\-path does not exist instead of creating it for the probe

.TP
\fB\-\-eb\fR \fI\,EB\/\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-require\-eb\fR
refuse when the EasyBuild command is not available

.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'eb\-staged\-rebuild run'\/\fR
usage: eb\-staged\-rebuild run [\-h] [\-\-software SOFTWARE] [\-\-modules MODULES]
                             [\-\-state\-root STATE_ROOT] [\-\-eb EB]
                             [\-\-backend {auto,bwrap,userns,installpath}]
                             [\-\-grace\-hours GRACE_HOURS] [\-\-dry\-run]
                             [\-\-module NAME/VERSION] [\-\-run\-id RUN_ID]
                             [\-\-lock\-timeout LOCK_TIMEOUT] [\-\-skip\-live\-check]
                             [\-\-prepare PREPARE]
                             [\-\-ledger\-config LEDGER_CONFIG] [\-\-build\-dir DIR]
                             [\-\-min\-free\-bytes BYTES] [\-\-require\-exchange]
                             [\-\-verify] [\-\-force]
                             ...

.TP
\fBeb_args\fR
easyconfig and eb options, after \-\-

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'eb\-staged\-rebuild run'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-software\fR \fI\,SOFTWARE\/\fR
live EASYBUILD_INSTALLPATH_SOFTWARE

.TP
\fB\-\-modules\fR \fI\,MODULES\/\fR
live EASYBUILD_INSTALLPATH_MODULES

.TP
\fB\-\-state\-root\fR \fI\,STATE_ROOT\/\fR
journal and stage root (default: <parent of software>/.eb\-staged\-rebuild)

.TP
\fB\-\-eb\fR \fI\,EB\/\fR
EasyBuild executable

.TP
\fB\-\-backend\fR \fI\,{auto,bwrap,userns,installpath}\/\fR
build isolation: auto tries bwrap, then a read\-only user namespace, then the
unsandboxed install\-path fallback

.TP
\fB\-\-grace\-hours\fR \fI\,GRACE_HOURS\/\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-module\fR \fI\,NAME/VERSION\/\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-run\-id\fR \fI\,RUN_ID\/\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-lock\-timeout\fR \fI\,LOCK_TIMEOUT\/\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-live\-check\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-prepare\fR \fI\,PREPARE\/\fR
executable called with a directory\-swap context JSON before the live directory
is exchanged

.TP
\fB\-\-ledger\-config\fR \fI\,LEDGER_CONFIG\/\fR
JSON eb\-stack ledger configuration; started records precede the directory swap

.TP
\fB\-\-build\-dir\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR
scratch build directory passed to eb as \-\-buildpath

.TP
\fB\-\-min\-free\-bytes\fR \fI\,BYTES\/\fR
refuse before the build unless the generation filesystem has at least BYTES
available

.TP
\fB\-\-require\-exchange\fR
refuse unless publication can use RENAME_EXCHANGE

.TP
\fB\-\-verify\fR
check the stage before the swap, and do not publish one that fails

.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
with \-\-verify, publish a stage that fails; the journal records it

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'eb\-staged\-rebuild resume'\/\fR
usage: eb\-staged\-rebuild resume [\-h] \-\-state\-root STATE_ROOT
                                [\-\-lock\-timeout LOCK_TIMEOUT] [\-\-verify]
                                [\-\-force]
                                run_id

.TP
\fBrun_id\fR

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'eb\-staged\-rebuild resume'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-state\-root\fR \fI\,STATE_ROOT\/\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-lock\-timeout\fR \fI\,LOCK_TIMEOUT\/\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-verify\fR
check the stage before the swap, as run \-\-verify does

.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
with \-\-verify, publish a stage that fails; the journal records it

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'eb\-staged\-rebuild verify'\/\fR
usage: eb\-staged\-rebuild verify [\-h] \-\-state\-root STATE_ROOT
                                [\-\-lock\-timeout LOCK_TIMEOUT]
                                STAGE

.TP
\fBSTAGE\fR
the run id that names the stage

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'eb\-staged\-rebuild verify'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-state\-root\fR \fI\,STATE_ROOT\/\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-lock\-timeout\fR \fI\,LOCK_TIMEOUT\/\fR

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'eb\-staged\-rebuild rollback'\/\fR
usage: eb\-staged\-rebuild rollback [\-h] \-\-state\-root STATE_ROOT
                                  [\-\-lock\-timeout LOCK_TIMEOUT] [\-\-to GEN]
                                  [\-\-latest]
                                  run_id

.TP
\fBrun_id\fR
the run to roll back, unless \-\-latest or \-\-to is given

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'eb\-staged\-rebuild rollback'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-state\-root\fR \fI\,STATE_ROOT\/\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-lock\-timeout\fR \fI\,LOCK_TIMEOUT\/\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-to\fR \fI\,GEN\/\fR
roll back every run published over run GEN

.TP
\fB\-\-latest\fR
roll back the newest complete run

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'eb\-staged\-rebuild gc'\/\fR
usage: eb\-staged\-rebuild gc [\-h] \-\-state\-root STATE_ROOT
                            [\-\-grace\-hours GRACE_HOURS] [\-\-dry\-run]
                            [\-\-lock\-timeout LOCK_TIMEOUT]
                            [\-\-usage\-log USAGE_LOG]
                            [\-\-eb\-keep\-logs EB_KEEP_LOGS]
                            [\-\-metrics\-file PATH] [\-\-include\-failed] [\-\-json]
                            [\-\-keep N] [\-\-check\-in\-use]

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'eb\-staged\-rebuild gc'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-state\-root\fR \fI\,STATE_ROOT\/\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-grace\-hours\fR \fI\,GRACE_HOURS\/\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-lock\-timeout\fR \fI\,LOCK_TIMEOUT\/\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-usage\-log\fR \fI\,USAGE_LOG\/\fR
usage log checked with eb\-keep\-logs used \-\-require\-none

.TP
\fB\-\-eb\-keep\-logs\fR \fI\,EB_KEEP_LOGS\/\fR
eb\-keep\-logs executable

.TP
\fB\-\-metrics\-file\fR \fI\,PATH\/\fR
atomically write Prometheus metrics after garbage collection

.TP
\fB\-\-include\-failed\fR
also remove the hidden trees and generation of a failed run that published
nothing, after the grace period

.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
write collection actions as JSON

.TP
\fB\-\-keep\fR \fI\,N\/\fR
keep each install path's N newest generations that rollback can switch back to

.TP
\fB\-\-check\-in\-use\fR
keep a tree or generation that a process or a mount on this node uses

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'eb\-staged\-rebuild retire'\/\fR
usage: eb\-staged\-rebuild retire [\-h] \-\-state\-root STATE_ROOT
                                \-\-module\-file MODULE_FILE [\-\-reason REASON]
                                [\-\-dry\-run] [\-\-usage\-log USAGE_LOG]
                                [\-\-eb\-keep\-logs EB_KEEP_LOGS]
                                [\-\-lock\-timeout LOCK_TIMEOUT]

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'eb\-staged\-rebuild retire'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-state\-root\fR \fI\,STATE_ROOT\/\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-module\-file\fR \fI\,MODULE_FILE\/\fR
module file to retire

.TP
\fB\-\-reason\fR \fI\,REASON\/\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-usage\-log\fR \fI\,USAGE_LOG\/\fR
usage log checked with eb\-keep\-logs used \-\-require\-none

.TP
\fB\-\-eb\-keep\-logs\fR \fI\,EB_KEEP_LOGS\/\fR
eb\-keep\-logs executable

.TP
\fB\-\-lock\-timeout\fR \fI\,LOCK_TIMEOUT\/\fR
seconds to wait for the lock (default: refuse at once)

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'eb\-staged\-rebuild status'\/\fR
usage: eb\-staged\-rebuild status [\-h] \-\-state\-root STATE_ROOT [\-\-json] [run_id]

.TP
\fBrun_id\fR

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'eb\-staged\-rebuild status'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-state\-root\fR \fI\,STATE_ROOT\/\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
print one JSON document

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'eb\-staged\-rebuild list'\/\fR
usage: eb\-staged\-rebuild list [\-h] \-\-state\-root STATE_ROOT

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'eb\-staged\-rebuild list'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-state\-root\fR \fI\,STATE_ROOT\/\fR

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'eb\-staged\-rebuild resolve'\/\fR
usage: eb\-staged\-rebuild resolve [\-h] module

.TP
\fBmodule\fR

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
show program's version number and exit

.SH AUTHOR
.nf
Rohit Goswami
.fi

.SH DISTRIBUTION
The latest version of eb\-staged\-rebuild may be downloaded from
.UR https://github.com/stackhands/eb\-staged\-rebuild
.UE
